    "title": "Nashville's Brandy Clark will perform at free outdoor concert in Galva - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Linda Cook ,\n4 hours ago\nCrossroads Cultural Connections has announced that Brandy Clark, one of Nashville’s most celebrated and respected singer-songwriters, will perform a free outdoor concert at Wiley Park in Galva at 5 p.m. Sunday, Oct. 12, a news release says.\nBrandy Clark (Crossroads Cultural Connections) This all-ages show is part of Crossroads Cultural Connections’ ongoing mission to bring world-class live music experiences to the area.\nGuests are encouraged to bring lawn chairs or blankets for comfortable seating on the grass. Food and drinks will be available for purchase from Snazzy’s Lemonade and Azteca de Oro. The evening will open with a performance by the indie-folk duo High Tea.\nBrandy Clark is a Grammy-winning artist and one of the most acclaimed songwriters in modern country music, known for her sharp wit, emotional depth, and authentic storytelling. A 12-time Grammy nominee, Clark won Best Americana Performance at the 2024 Grammy Awards for her hauntingly beautiful song “Dear Insecurity,” featuring Brandi Carlile — who also produced her most recent self-titled album.\nClark’s songs, both as a performer and songwriter for other artists, have helped define a new era of country and Americana music. She’s written chart-topping hits for stars including Miranda Lambert (“Mama’s Broken Heart”), The Band Perry (“Better Dig Two”), Kacey Musgraves (“Follow Your Arrow” and “Biscuits”), Reba McEntire, and Darius Rucker, among many others.\nHer solo albums — including “12 Stories,” “Big Day in a Small Town,” “Your Life Is a Record,” and “Brandy Clark” — have received widespread critical acclaim from outlets such as NPR, Rolling Stone, and The New York Times, which hailed her as “one of country’s greatest storytellers.”\nWith her powerful voice, sharp lyricism, and compassionate character studies of everyday people, Clark has earned a reputation as an artist who bridges traditional country roots with a contemporary Americana sound — one that resonates deeply with fans across generations.\nFor more information visit here .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHBF - OurQuadCities.com.",
